  <data name="ProviderSteps_google" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open the Google Cloud console and create an OAuth client of type “Web application”.
Add the return address to the authorized redirect URIs.
Paste the client ID and secret here.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ProviderSteps_microsoft" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Register an app in Microsoft Entra ID with the platform “Web”.
Add the return address as a redirect URI.
Create a client secret and paste it here with the application (client) ID.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ProviderSteps_github" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open GitHub → Settings → Developer settings and create an OAuth App.
Set the return address as the authorization callback URL.
Generate a client secret and paste it here with the client ID.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ProviderSteps_gitlab" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open GitLab → Preferences → Applications and add an application.
Set the return address as the redirect URI and tick the scope read_user.
Paste the application ID and secret here.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ProviderSteps_yandex" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create an app at oauth.yandex.ru with the platform “Web services”.
Set the return address as the callback URL and allow access to the login and e-mail.
Paste the ID and password here.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ProviderSteps_vkid" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create an app in VK ID for business with the platform “Web”.
Add the return address as a trusted redirect URL.
Paste the app ID and the protected key here.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ProviderSteps_discord" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open the Discord developer portal and create an application.
Add the return address in OAuth2 → Redirects.
Paste the client ID and secret here.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ProviderSteps_telegram" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open @BotFather, choose your bot and set up “Log in with Telegram”.
Add the return address to the allowed URLs.
Paste the client ID and secret here.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ProviderSteps_oidc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create an OpenID Connect client in your identity provider (Keycloak, Authentik, Okta and others).
Add the return address as a redirect URI.
Paste the issuer address, the client ID and the secret here.</value>
  </data>
